CQ number 3 for the pizza ontology is:  
**"Which pizzas are vegetarian?"**

This competency question can be answered using the class `:VegetarianPizza`, which is defined as any pizza that does not have a fish topping and does not have a meat topping. In OWL, this is represented as:

```
:VegetarianPizza rdf:type owl:Class ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ owl:intersectionOf ( :Pizza
        [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
          owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                             owl:onProperty :hasTopping ;
                             owl:someValuesFrom :FishTopping
                           ]
        ]
        [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
          owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                             owl:onProperty :hasTopping ;
                             owl:someValuesFrom :MeatTopping
                           ]
        ]
      ) ;
      rdf:type owl:Class
    ] ;
    rdfs:comment "Any pizza that does not have fish topping and does not have meat topping is a VegetarianPizza. Members of this class do not need to have any toppings at all."@en ;
    rdfs:label "PizzaVegetariana"@pt .
```

To answer the question, retrieve all individuals or subclasses of `:VegetarianPizza`.

