CQ number 12 for the pizza ontology is: Which pizzas are sharing all their toppings with other pizzas?

In the context of the pizza ontology, this competency question asks: For which pizzas does every topping also appear as a topping on at least one other pizza? In other words, there is no unique topping on these pizzas; all their toppings are shared with at least one other pizza.

This can be formalized as:  
Find all instances of :Pizza such that for every topping t (where the pizza :hasTopping t), there exists another pizza p2 (p2 ≠ p1) such that p2 :hasTopping t.

SPARQL-style pseudo-query:
```
SELECT ?pizza
WHERE {
  ?pizza a :Pizza .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pizza :hasTopping ?topping .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?otherPizza a :Pizza .
      FILTER (?otherPizza != ?pizza) .
      ?otherPizza :hasTopping ?topping .
    }
  }
}
```
This query returns all pizzas where every topping is also found on another pizza.

Is pizza a subclass of food?

Yes, in the pizza ontology, :Pizza is defined as a subclass of :Food:

:Pizza rdf:type owl:Class ;
       rdfs:subClassOf :Food ,
                       [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                         owl:onProperty :hasBase ;
                         owl:someValuesFrom :PizzaBase
                       ] ;
       owl:disjointWith :PizzaBase ,
                        :PizzaTopping ;
       rdfs:label "Pizza"@en .

